\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The standard derivative-based parser. The forward pass stores the residual after each character in \texttt  {expressions}, entry $i$ being the residual after $i$ characters, and returns \texttt  {None} if the final entry is not nullable. The backward pass starts from \texttt  {mk\_eps} of the final entry and applies \texttt  {inject} to the preceding entries in reverse, yielding the parse tree for $r$.}}{31}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deriv-std-drivers-rust}{{5.4}{31}{The standard derivative-based parser. The forward pass stores the residual after each character in \texttt {expressions}, entry $i$ being the residual after $i$ characters, and returns \texttt {None} if the final entry is not nullable. The backward pass starts from \texttt {mk\_eps} of the final entry and applies \texttt {inject} to the preceding entries in reverse, yielding the parse tree for $r$}{figure.caption.18}{}}
